title: Fields in groups
intro: Big components put their fields under subheadings that fold, and fields fade while what they need is off.
project: Platformer | Field Groups

chapter: Subheadings | Big components, in sections you can fold
select: Player
say: Platformer Movement has twenty six fields. They used to be one long list. Now they sit under subheadings.
explain: group:PlatformerMovement.Jump | Jump | Everything about jumping is under Jump: how high, air jumps, coyote time, and how it falls.
explain: group:PlatformerMovement.Dash | Dash | The dash has its own subheading, and so do walls, ladders, control, and sounds.
say: Not making a game with a dash? Fold it shut.
click: fold:PlatformerMovement.Dash
expectfolded: PlatformerMovement.Dash = true
say: It stays folded on every entity with Platformer Movement, and next time the editor starts, until you open it again.

chapter: Fields that wait | Faded until what they need is on
click: fold:PlatformerMovement.Dash
expectfolded: PlatformerMovement.Dash = false
expectfaded: PlatformerMovement.DashSpeed = false
say: This player can dash, so its dash speed, time and cooldown are in use.
set: PlatformerMovement.Dash = false
expectvalue: Player.PlatformerMovement.Dash = false
expectfaded: PlatformerMovement.DashSpeed = true
explain: field:PlatformerMovement.DashSpeed | Faded | Untick Dash, and its fields fade. They do nothing until it's back on.
tip: label:PlatformerMovement.DashSpeed
say: Its name says what it's waiting for. You can still set it ahead of time.
set: PlatformerMovement.Dash = true
expectfaded: PlatformerMovement.DashSpeed = false
say: Tick Dash again, and they come back.
expectfaded: PlatformerMovement.WallSlideSpeed = true
explain: field:PlatformerMovement.WallSlideSpeed | Wall Slide Speed | Wall slide speed waits for Wall Slide the same way. Buttons do it too: a button's scene only lights up when its action loads one.
say: Subheadings to find things, and faded fields to show what's in use. Agents see the same groups when they describe a component.
